{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>YHWH, the Elohim of heaven, who took me from my father's house.</b> And He did not say 'and the Elohim of the earth,' while above He said ״I make you swear״ etc.? He said to him: Now He is Elohim of heaven and Elohim of earth, for I have made Him habitual in the mouths of people; but when He took me from my father's house, He was Elohim of heaven and not Elohim of earth, for the people of the world did not recognize Him and His name was not habitual in the earth." "<b>From my father's house.</b> From Charan." "<b>And from the land of my birth.</b> From Ur Kasdim." "<b>Who spoke to me.</b> For my needs — as in ״אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר עָלָיו״ (I Kings 2), and so all לִי and לוֹ and לָהֶם attached to דִּבּוּר are explicated in the sense of עַל, and their Targum is עֲלַי, עֲלוֹהִי, עֲלֵיהוֹן — for לִי and לוֹ and לָהֶם do not attach to דִּבּוּר in the sense of אֵלַי, אֵלָיו, אֲלֵיהֶם, whose Targum is עִמִּי, עִמֵּיהּ, עִמְּהוֹן; but with אֲמִירָה, לִי and לוֹ and לָהֶם do attach." "<b>And who swore to me.</b> Between the pieces."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:09.754528197Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}